NAME

ulibGetMsgData - Returns information about a message


SYNOPSIS

long ulibGetMsgData(struct Msg *m, long AccessType, long *DataSize)
                          a0             d0               a1


DESCRIPTION

This function returns information about the message pointed to by <m>.

The <AccessType> parameter may be any one of the #define'd XMD_ codes in
xenolink.h (such as XMD_NUMBER, XMD_SECTION, XMD_TO_USER, etc.)

<DataSize> is valid only for the string variables:

   XMD_FROM_USER      Message author
   XMD_TO_USER        Message recipient
   XMD_SUBJECT        Message subject

If <DataSize> is not NULL, it should point to a long integer into which the
maximum allowable length of the string (including null terminator) will be
placed (e.g. USERNAME_LENGTH).


NOTES

Usage of <DataSize> is unnecessary and not recommended, since the maximum
string lengths of message data strings is provided in xenolink.h.  These
numbers are highly unlikely to change!


RETURNS

This function returns the requested information as either:

   1. A signed long integer (for integral message fields)
      (Note that all integral return values are promoted to signed long
      integers)

   2. A pointer to a string (for string variables such as To, From, Subject)

   3. A pointer to a (struct TimeDate) (for XMD_DATE_SENT, XMD_DATE_RECEIVED).


SEE ALSO

